      "message": "OK, I looked into this and the root of the problem when including hooks/dtask.h in linux/percpu-rwsem.h is the following cyclic dependency:\n\n - linux/percpu-rwsem.h\n - hooks/dtask.h\n - trace/define_trace.h\n - trace/trace_events.h\n - linux/trace_events.h\n - linux/ring_buffer.h\n - linux/mm.h\n - linux/huge_mm.h\n - linux/fs.h\n - linux/percpu-rwsem.h\n\nFixing this is probably going to require to big of a surgery, so putting things out of line is probably simpler. But please:\n 1. rename your out-of-line function as _trace_android_vh_record_lock_starttime() so it is obvious what it is\n 2. add a comment above that function explaining why this is needed\n 3. remove the unecessary ifdefery from dtask.h (we don\u0027t include it from a header file in the end)",
